It is Saturday, and I am relaxing on my sofa.
I start a video call to my family in Mexico.
My mother answers almost immediately.
"Hello Maya, my darling," she says with a big smile.
I can see my sister Sofía and our dog Lola in the background.
"Hello mom."
"Things are going really well here," I say happily.
We talk a bit about their week back home in Mexico.
Then my mother looks curiously at me.
"But what was actually the hardest thing in January?" she asks.
I think back on my early days in the city.
Everything was new, and the days were sometimes difficult.
"The beginning was not always easy," I tell her.
"I waited in a long queue a whole morning."
"I sat in an empty kitchen and missed you."
"I took the wrong bus one Saturday and got lost."
"And I froze incredibly much without a good jacket," I add.
My mother listens attentively and nods.
She really wants to hear all the stories from my start in Denmark.
I take a sip of my tea and continue my story.
